  "cases": [
    {
      "schema": "nlp-eval/2",
      "id": "archive-discourse-dialogue/connected-chat",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "text": "user: We want a formalizer that converts English requests into a canonical controlled language.\nuser: Every candidate formalization must preserve negation, modality, quantifiers, temporal order, and references.\nuser: If the symbolic parser is uncertain, mark the ambiguity instead of guessing.\nuser: Find three difficult examples involving pronouns and modal scope.\nuser: Do not include examples that require specialist medical knowledge.\nuser: Bob told Alan that he should review the report.\nuser: I mean Alan.\nuser: Not every reviewer must accept a paper.\nuser: Does that mean some reviewer is not required to accept a paper?\nuser: Before Ada approves the report, Bob must review it.\nuser: If Bob rejects it, Ada should not publish it.\nuser: Which report is being discussed?\nuser: Use the report from the previous example.\nuser: The evaluator may accept a candidate only if no material meaning is missing.\nuser: It may reject a candidate because the CNL invents a condition that is not present in the source.\nuser: If the source is ambiguous and the context does not resolve it, the evaluator must return uncertain.\nuser: Show me which candidates were rejected and why.\nuser: Keep the explanation short, but preserve the exact evidence spans.\nuser: We prefer one batched LLM call over one call per sentence.\nuser: When ten candidates are ready, validate them together.\nuser: Do not wait for ten if the user explicitly asks for an immediate verdict.\nuser: A candidate that passes the symbolic audit can still be wrong.\nuser: Therefore sample some apparently safe candidates for LLM review.\nuser: How many of the last twenty candidates were judged equivalent?\nuser: If fewer than eighteen were equivalent, report the failure rate.\nuser: The judge must not use world knowledge to fill missing information.\nuser: Only information licensed by the source or the conversation may be used.\nuser: Can the formalizer distinguish 'does not have to submit' from 'must not submit'?\nuser: Test both readings and mark any scope error.\nuser: Finally, return the CNL, the symbolic warnings, and the LLM verdict for each tested turn.",
      "category": "discourse/connected-dialogue",
      "tags": [],
      "turns": [
        {
          "id": "t01",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "We want a formalizer that converts English requests into a canonical controlled language."
        },
        {
          "id": "t02",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Every candidate formalization must preserve negation, modality, quantifiers, temporal order, and references."
        },
        {
          "id": "t03",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "If the symbolic parser is uncertain, mark the ambiguity instead of guessing."
        },
        {
          "id": "t04",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Find three difficult examples involving pronouns and modal scope."
        },
        {
          "id": "t05",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Do not include examples that require specialist medical knowledge."
        },
        {
          "id": "t06",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Bob told Alan that he should review the report."
        },
        {
          "id": "t07",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "I mean Alan."
        },
        {
          "id": "t08",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Not every reviewer must accept a paper."
        },
        {
          "id": "t09",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Does that mean some reviewer is not required to accept a paper?"
        },
        {
          "id": "t10",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Before Ada approves the report, Bob must review it."
        },
        {
          "id": "t11",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "If Bob rejects it, Ada should not publish it."
        },
        {
          "id": "t12",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Which report is being discussed?"
        },
        {
          "id": "t13",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Use the report from the previous example."
        },
        {
          "id": "t14",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "The evaluator may accept a candidate only if no material meaning is missing."
        },
        {
          "id": "t15",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "It may reject a candidate because the CNL invents a condition that is not present in the source."
        },
        {
          "id": "t16",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "If the source is ambiguous and the context does not resolve it, the evaluator must return uncertain."
        },
        {
          "id": "t17",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Show me which candidates were rejected and why."
        },
        {
          "id": "t18",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Keep the explanation short, but preserve the exact evidence spans."
        },
        {
          "id": "t19",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "We prefer one batched LLM call over one call per sentence."
        },
        {
          "id": "t20",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "When ten candidates are ready, validate them together."
        },
        {
          "id": "t21",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Do not wait for ten if the user explicitly asks for an immediate verdict."
        },
        {
          "id": "t22",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "A candidate that passes the symbolic audit can still be wrong."
        },
        {
          "id": "t23",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Therefore sample some apparently safe candidates for LLM review."
        },
        {
          "id": "t24",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "How many of the last twenty candidates were judged equivalent?"
        },
        {
          "id": "t25",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "If fewer than eighteen were equivalent, report the failure rate."
        },
        {
          "id": "t26",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "The judge must not use world knowledge to fill missing information."
        },
        {
          "id": "t27",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Only information licensed by the source or the conversation may be used."
        },
        {
          "id": "t28",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Can the formalizer distinguish 'does not have to submit' from 'must not submit'?"
        },
        {
          "id": "t29",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Test both readings and mark any scope error."
        },
        {
          "id": "t30",
          "speaker": "user",
          "text": "Finally, return the CNL, the symbolic warnings, and the LLM verdict for each tested turn."
        }
      ],
